                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_100">Cambridge, Cambridgeshire.
                        Gonville Hall. </orgName><p>‘Gunvile hall’ (flyleaf)</p><p>The text is in
                        the MS attributed to ‘Freculfus’, in reponse to which a s. xv hand has
                        written ‘credo quod mentiris’. Cf. Stegmüller, Bibl., no. 10881; Madrid BN
                        MS 5992, fol. 67; and Bamberg Staatsbibl. MS Patr. 64, fol. 170v; with each
                        of which it shares an incipit (of text or of prologue)</p><p>James, Gonville
                        and Caius, 91, states that the inscription ‘Gunvile hall’ ‘is written in all
                        of Grene’s books’, referring to William Grene</p></provenance>
